course: dictionary
lesson: 13932
title: Leisure
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Leisure means free time. It is the time when you are not at school, not working and not doing homework, so you can do what you enjoy. «On Saturday, Sam has plenty of leisure time to play in the park.» Sam is free to choose what to do, so leisure means free time.
explain: Leisure can also describe things that are for relaxing and fun. «The leisure centre has a big swimming pool.» Here leisure tells you what kind of centre it is: a place for fun and sport.
explain: The phrase at your leisure means when it suits you, with no set time. «You can pay the bill at your leisure.» There is no rush, so you choose the time.
fact: Leisure means free time when you are not working or studying.
fact: Leisure activities are things you do for fun, such as hobbies, sport or reading.
fact: A leisure centre is a place with things like a swimming pool and sports halls.
fact: «At your leisure» means when it suits you.
fact: Leisure is an uncountable noun, so you say «some leisure», not «a leisure».
exercise: «On Saturday, Sam has plenty of leisure time.» What does leisure mean here? | Time spent doing homework | Time spent at school | A type of sports shoe | *Free time to do what you enjoy
exercise: «The leisure centre has a big swimming pool.» What kind of centre is it? | A shop that sells food | A place for sleeping | *A place for fun and sport | A school for maths
exercise: The bar chart shows the hours of leisure each child has on Sunday. What is leisure in this problem? | Hours spent doing homework | The number of children in the class | *Free time when you are not working or studying | Hours spent travelling to school
test: «You can pay the bill at your leisure.» What does at your leisure mean? | Never, at any time | *When it suits you | As quickly as possible | At exactly nine o'clock
test: Which of these is a leisure activity? | Writing a list of spelling words | Sweeping the classroom floor | Doing a maths test | *Reading a book for fun
exam: Which word means free time for fun? | *leisure | work | homework | lesson
